  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2} & =c \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equations $y=\\pm \\sqrt{c}$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [0,\\infty ),$ the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14143522/assets/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
